main.go:421, :570: tailLines(res.Output, 300) leaves no marker; the agent gets exit 0 plus lines 101..400 and cannot know that 100 lines vanished (compile errors above the tail). Observed: 400-line command -> 302 lines returned starting at 101. main.go:391 + supervisor.go:118: logs has a hard 500-line ring buffer and a larger lines argument is clipped without a marker (observed lines=1000 on a 600-line producer -> 500 lines).
Acceptance: a '[... N lines omitted]' prefix when cut, optionally a lines argument and a byte cap for run_*; logs says 'last 500 of buffer' or the buffer size is configurable; tests.
